WEBVTT

00:11.011 --> 00:15.015
NOTES FROM THE LAST ROW

00:17.767 --> 00:18.893
I knew they'd do it.

00:21.312 --> 00:22.814
-Hello, sir.
-Yeah.

00:25.400 --> 00:29.738
YEONSEO UNIVERSITY
PROGRAMMING COMPETITION RESULTS

00:34.117 --> 00:36.077
KIM SE-YUN, LEE KANG

00:36.661 --> 00:39.122
RUNNER-UP

00:42.375 --> 00:43.376
Mr. Heo.

00:43.960 --> 00:44.961
Jesus Christ!

00:45.045 --> 00:46.838
It's just me. Why are you so surprised?

00:48.548 --> 00:51.426
I was going to tell you,
but you've already seen.

00:55.138 --> 00:56.139
Hey.

00:56.931 --> 00:59.100
Why are you runner-up?
You knew the problems.

00:59.184 --> 01:03.354
I threw a few of the problems.
If we won, we'd be going to the finals.

01:04.272 --> 01:05.607
That wouldn't be fair.

01:09.152 --> 01:10.195
I'm going

01:10.695 --> 01:12.238
to Se-yun's house tomorrow.

01:12.739 --> 01:14.240
To have dinner with them.

01:15.200 --> 01:16.201
I was invited.

01:18.411 --> 01:19.245
I see.

01:20.038 --> 01:22.540
Then our lessons will start this weekend.

01:23.750 --> 01:25.794
Submit your assignment
by email before then.

01:25.877 --> 01:26.795
Okay.

01:27.295 --> 01:28.463
See you Saturday, then.

01:30.381 --> 01:31.382
Hey, Lee Kang.

01:38.431 --> 01:40.517
You do know this has to be our secret?

01:40.600 --> 01:42.310
It stays between us.

01:42.393 --> 01:43.478
I know.

02:01.287 --> 02:02.914
-Hello, sir.
-Yeah, hi!

02:04.541 --> 02:06.668
The act of writing itself helps you think…

02:06.751 --> 02:08.795
…no complete blueprint in your mind.

02:08.878 --> 02:11.214
It's akin to going on a journey
without a map.

02:13.550 --> 02:15.135
Yes, well…

02:15.218 --> 02:17.720
If I push a large door open and enter,

02:18.388 --> 02:20.306
only to find another smaller door,

02:20.890 --> 02:22.851
did I ever really step inside,

02:23.560 --> 02:25.311
or was I outside all along?

02:29.107 --> 02:30.275
A smaller door?

02:46.374 --> 02:47.208
How thoughtful.

02:48.626 --> 02:51.004
How did you know
that Yun's mom likes white roses?

02:51.671 --> 02:54.674
Yun told me, actually.

02:56.926 --> 02:58.678
But I could only afford three.

03:00.263 --> 03:02.307
How's the food? Do you like it?

03:02.390 --> 03:05.393
Yes, it's delicious.
I'm enjoying all of it.

03:05.476 --> 03:07.061
Thank you for inviting me.

03:07.562 --> 03:10.773
Not at all.
We should be the ones thanking you.

03:10.857 --> 03:13.318
Thanks to you, Kang, our Yun won an award.

03:13.401 --> 03:14.569
Runner-up, no less.

03:15.069 --> 03:17.363
We never expected that much.

03:17.864 --> 03:20.825
Please take good care of our Yun.

03:22.702 --> 03:24.662
Kang, do you have any siblings?

03:25.413 --> 03:26.247
Sorry?

03:29.167 --> 03:30.376
Oh, siblings?

03:31.085 --> 03:32.086
It's just me.

03:32.170 --> 03:33.630
So you're an only child.

03:34.130 --> 03:37.050
Where do your parents live?
What do they do?

03:40.303 --> 03:42.931
A mother bird's anxious efforts
to protect her young.

03:44.807 --> 03:46.476
The second door I encountered.

03:46.976 --> 03:49.229
Goodness, honey.

03:49.896 --> 03:51.522
Why would you ask him that?

03:52.815 --> 03:53.942
I just…

03:54.025 --> 03:57.028
Wait, was that rude of me?
Is it not okay to ask?

03:57.111 --> 04:00.323
Kang doesn't talk about himself much.
He doesn't like to.

04:00.823 --> 04:01.658
Is that so?

04:02.158 --> 04:05.912
I see. Then I guess that was rude of me.

04:05.995 --> 04:06.829
I'm sorry.

04:07.705 --> 04:08.873
My apologies.

04:09.749 --> 04:12.252
If we're all done eating,
should we have dessert?

04:12.335 --> 04:13.836
-Yeah.
-Fruit? Or cake?

04:14.921 --> 04:16.047
I don't have a mom.

04:20.969 --> 04:22.345
I needed a key.

04:22.887 --> 04:25.139
A key that could unlock that door.

04:25.223 --> 04:27.600
She left us when I was eight.

04:31.187 --> 04:34.440
My dad got hurt doing construction work
and was sick for a long time.

04:35.817 --> 04:38.653
He's in a nursing home now
due to alcohol-induced dementia.

04:42.323 --> 04:43.241
Then…

04:44.951 --> 04:46.577
who did you live with?

04:47.078 --> 04:48.788
-Honey.
-It's all right.

04:50.581 --> 04:51.666
I understand your curiosity.

04:54.043 --> 04:56.796
Yes, I'm asking
because I'm genuinely worried.

04:56.879 --> 04:58.840
I wonder who took care of him.

04:58.923 --> 05:00.800
Any parental figures.

05:01.759 --> 05:02.593
I did.

05:05.388 --> 05:06.639
I took care of myself

05:07.932 --> 05:09.017
and my dad.

05:12.312 --> 05:14.939
It was just us two
until he was hospitalized.

05:15.023 --> 05:18.318
From second grade
until I started university.

05:19.569 --> 05:21.070
Goodness.

05:21.571 --> 05:22.613
So,

05:23.656 --> 05:25.992
you studied while taking care of your dad

05:26.492 --> 05:28.119
and still got into Yeonseo?

05:28.786 --> 05:31.497
Kang's grades even got him
a full scholarship.

05:32.165 --> 05:33.166
Right?

05:33.249 --> 05:34.876
I worked really hard.

05:36.627 --> 05:38.588
I didn't want people to know my situation.

05:40.048 --> 05:42.425
Nor did I want to be a burden to anyone.

05:42.508 --> 05:46.220
So I studied like crazy
between my part-time jobs.

05:48.639 --> 05:50.850
But I don't feel alone anymore.

05:53.978 --> 05:55.521
Because I made a friend.

05:57.148 --> 05:59.192
Someone who's completely
different from me.

06:01.986 --> 06:03.905
He's so bright and carefree.

06:04.530 --> 06:08.326
Looking at him is like looking at
a clear blue sky without a single cloud.

06:10.495 --> 06:12.288
Yet he also has a big heart.

06:13.081 --> 06:15.083
At first, I was simply fascinated.

06:16.084 --> 06:18.127
Wondering how he grew up to be like that.

06:19.295 --> 06:21.547
But it clicked after I visited his home.

06:24.008 --> 06:26.135
Why he was so different.

06:29.430 --> 06:30.431
It was his family.

06:32.975 --> 06:34.811
Thanks to his loving family

06:35.728 --> 06:38.689
and thanks to him,
I think I'm starting to understand

06:40.358 --> 06:41.859
what makes a home

06:43.236 --> 06:44.779
and what family truly means.

06:47.407 --> 06:49.075
I'm learning a little every day.

06:54.664 --> 06:55.790
Oh my.

06:56.833 --> 06:58.334
Goodness, young man.

06:58.960 --> 07:02.046
You thought all that
every time you visited our home?

07:07.718 --> 07:10.680
You know what, Kang?
You're not alone anymore.

07:13.099 --> 07:14.600
Don't you understand?

07:15.101 --> 07:17.770
I'm saying you can come over
whenever you want.

07:18.646 --> 07:20.606
Consider this place your home.

07:21.482 --> 07:23.734
You're practically family now.

07:27.738 --> 07:29.907
I only realized after opening the door

07:30.658 --> 07:33.327
which door it was
that I had truly wanted to open.

07:36.664 --> 07:38.040
The door to their hearts.

07:38.749 --> 07:42.670
Only then does the divide
between the inside and out disappear.

07:46.215 --> 07:49.719
P.S. I owe all of this to you, Mr. Heo.

07:50.219 --> 07:52.430
None of this would have been possible

07:52.513 --> 07:54.765
if you hadn't slipped me
the competition problems.

07:55.641 --> 07:57.852
Thank you, Mr. Heo.

08:07.695 --> 08:11.115
What are you doing here? Why did you
read this without my permission?

08:12.658 --> 08:15.453
What was that about competition problems?

08:16.412 --> 08:19.916
You slipped him the problems?
What on earth did you do?

08:21.459 --> 08:22.793
What problems?

08:23.961 --> 08:25.338
What are you talking about?

08:25.838 --> 08:27.215
You don't know, do you?

08:27.757 --> 08:30.301
That you wrinkle your nose when you lie.

08:31.761 --> 08:34.263
Enough. I have a lot to do. Get out.

08:37.850 --> 08:40.520
Look. It's written right here at the end.

08:41.437 --> 08:42.980
-Let go.
-Hand it here.

08:45.566 --> 08:46.567
Are you insane?

08:46.651 --> 08:49.779
So why lie? What did he mean
about competition problems?

08:49.862 --> 08:51.113
Just drop it!

08:51.614 --> 08:52.740
What's it to you?

08:54.992 --> 08:56.202
"What's it to you?"

08:57.995 --> 08:59.205
Please.

08:59.288 --> 09:01.207
Just leave me alone.

09:01.290 --> 09:03.251
Stop trying to know everything.

09:04.126 --> 09:07.129
And from now on,
don't come in here without permission.

09:07.213 --> 09:08.881
Or read my students' assignments.

09:10.967 --> 09:13.135
Just mind your own business!

09:19.684 --> 09:22.937
That damn lunatic.
Why did he even write that?

09:38.411 --> 09:39.453
Oh my God!

09:42.999 --> 09:45.543
What are you doing? You startled me.

09:48.087 --> 09:49.422
I called your name.

09:50.256 --> 09:51.549
And knocked.

09:53.467 --> 09:54.302
What?

09:54.802 --> 09:55.886
Why are you here?

10:03.144 --> 10:04.604
What are you doing?

10:11.819 --> 10:14.238
I don't recall saying you could lie down.

10:22.622 --> 10:23.748
Yeah.

10:25.666 --> 10:27.585
I did something bad.

10:30.046 --> 10:31.422
Lee Kang, that punk.

10:32.423 --> 10:33.758
They were problems

10:33.841 --> 10:36.510
for his programming competition
or whatever.

10:38.512 --> 10:40.181
I stole them and gave them to him.

10:43.726 --> 10:45.269
Don't ask any more questions.

10:46.354 --> 10:48.439
I just had to do it, so I did.

10:49.357 --> 10:51.067
What's that supposed to mean?

10:51.817 --> 10:52.735
But how…

10:53.444 --> 10:54.737
How could you…

10:57.823 --> 11:01.827
Whatever the reason, this isn't like you.
Stealing competition problems?

11:01.911 --> 11:03.371
I know that too.

11:05.790 --> 11:07.625
It wasn't like me.

11:12.046 --> 11:13.214
But…

11:17.802 --> 11:18.928
it was thrilling.

11:20.221 --> 11:21.055
What?

11:23.015 --> 11:24.975
That's what made it even more thrilling.

11:26.602 --> 11:28.354
It was something I'd never do.

11:30.940 --> 11:32.608
I'd never felt like that before.

11:41.575 --> 11:42.785
How should I put it?

11:43.619 --> 11:48.165
It felt like jumping over my own fence
for the first time in my life.

11:56.215 --> 11:59.093
Are you saying crossing the line
made you feel liberated?

12:00.386 --> 12:01.971
Someone as bullheaded as you?

12:02.847 --> 12:04.181
Liberation? Please.

12:05.057 --> 12:06.976
That's just how it felt at the time.

12:10.229 --> 12:13.482
Come to think of it,
you have been acting a little strange.

12:14.316 --> 12:15.735
Even now.

12:16.819 --> 12:18.654
You're lying here on my bed.

12:27.872 --> 12:29.290
You can sleep here.

12:34.462 --> 12:38.132
If you want to sleep here, you can.
I don't mind.

13:00.696 --> 13:01.781
How long has it been…

13:04.617 --> 13:07.787
since we started sleeping
in separate rooms?

13:09.663 --> 13:11.207
How long?

13:12.958 --> 13:14.126
Twelve years?

13:15.044 --> 13:17.046
No, it's been 13 years.

13:20.549 --> 13:22.134
It was since then.

13:23.719 --> 13:25.471
When we gave up on IVF.

14:35.457 --> 14:37.626
Eat this with Lee Kang when he gets here.

14:37.710 --> 14:39.670
Today is your first real lesson, isn't it?

14:40.170 --> 14:41.422
Okay, thanks.

14:41.922 --> 14:43.549
You should head out now.

14:46.010 --> 14:49.555
No, I don't have anywhere to be today.
I'll stay here with you.

14:51.432 --> 14:54.768
-You don't mean in this room, do you?
-Is that a problem?

14:54.852 --> 14:57.813
Why would you be here for the lesson?

14:58.397 --> 15:01.692
Why are you getting so worked up?
I was just kidding.

15:07.615 --> 15:09.366
Why are you getting all awkward?

15:09.992 --> 15:12.161
-You won't even look at me.
-As if.

15:14.163 --> 15:16.206
You haven't changed a bit.

15:17.166 --> 15:18.834
Though I did always find it cute.

15:18.918 --> 15:22.087
Come on.
Stop talking nonsense and get out.

15:22.171 --> 15:23.923
He'll be here any minute.

15:25.966 --> 15:27.551
Wait, I have a question.

15:28.719 --> 15:32.681
Did you know about
what Lee Kang wrote in his assignment?

15:33.474 --> 15:35.059
About his personal life.

15:35.976 --> 15:38.562
I felt bad for him
while reading that part.

15:39.271 --> 15:42.942
I didn't. He and I have never
talked about that stuff before.

15:44.026 --> 15:46.028
Never? Not even once?

15:48.906 --> 15:50.741
That's the problem with you.

15:50.824 --> 15:54.370
You're a writer who teaches literature,
yet you don't care about people.

15:54.453 --> 15:55.537
What could he learn?

15:57.623 --> 15:58.916
Here we go again!

16:01.710 --> 16:02.544
Please leave.

16:36.370 --> 16:37.830
What's with the flowers?

16:38.497 --> 16:42.543
Since today's lesson is in the morning,
I figured your wife would be home.

16:43.043 --> 16:45.713
I couldn't show up empty-handed
the first time we met.

16:46.213 --> 16:47.923
But they were expensive.

16:48.674 --> 16:50.009
I could only afford three.

16:51.885 --> 16:53.095
Are you kidding me?

16:54.388 --> 16:58.225
You wrote that in your assignment
about the three white roses.

17:01.895 --> 17:03.188
Right, so I did.

17:04.314 --> 17:06.775
But it's true. Roses are expensive.

17:08.652 --> 17:09.653
Whatever.

17:11.613 --> 17:12.573
Let me ask.

17:14.616 --> 17:17.286
What you wrote about your life
in your assignment,

17:18.287 --> 17:19.121
is it true?

17:26.628 --> 17:29.715
Are you asking if the narrator
in my assignment and the author

17:30.257 --> 17:32.301
are the same person?

17:33.552 --> 17:34.553
Then what?

17:35.929 --> 17:37.014
You made that up?

17:38.807 --> 17:41.226
Not exactly, but I don't know.

17:42.519 --> 17:44.855
They could be the same
yet different, you know?

17:45.731 --> 17:48.776
Is the narrator in your novel
the same person as the author?

17:50.819 --> 17:51.653
My novel?

17:51.737 --> 17:52.780
Yes.

17:53.489 --> 17:54.364
Your novel.

18:04.833 --> 18:05.709
TWELVE WOMEN

18:06.043 --> 18:09.129
I stumbled upon it
at a secondhand bookstore.

18:10.047 --> 18:12.132
I haven't finished it yet,

18:12.925 --> 18:17.262
but it seems to be about a man
who wanders between 12 different women.

18:17.763 --> 18:19.556
Let's stop talking about this book.

18:22.059 --> 18:23.102
This book is…

18:24.937 --> 18:26.772
too complex for you to understand yet.

18:29.942 --> 18:32.027
Actually, no one can understand it.

18:32.528 --> 18:36.073
No. Although it's a bit complex,
I'm finding it interesting.

18:39.451 --> 18:43.497
So is the narrator in this novel
the same person as the author?

18:44.123 --> 18:44.957
Well?

18:47.918 --> 18:49.545
I'm dying to know.

19:01.682 --> 19:02.891
Yeah.

19:04.893 --> 19:06.228
Just as you said…

19:11.066 --> 19:14.027
the author and the narrator
can indeed be identical,

19:15.320 --> 19:16.822
or they can be different.

19:19.199 --> 19:20.909
The twelve women

19:22.286 --> 19:24.037
were mere figments of my imagination.

19:31.503 --> 19:33.714
The truth is, it was about one woman.

19:35.966 --> 19:36.800
Sorry?

19:37.885 --> 19:38.719
What was that?

19:38.802 --> 19:39.928
Enough.

19:41.638 --> 19:43.599
Let's stop talking about narrators.

19:44.683 --> 19:46.727
Let's start the lesson. Put that away.

19:47.352 --> 19:50.105
-No, what did you just say?
-Put it away, please.

19:56.195 --> 20:00.157
I actually have something to tell you
before we start the lesson.

20:01.658 --> 20:02.784
Some good news.

20:04.161 --> 20:05.913
I'm moving

20:07.039 --> 20:08.457
into Se-yun's house.

20:10.167 --> 20:11.084
Moving in?

20:18.926 --> 20:22.804
It came up when we were eating
after a game of basketball.

20:23.305 --> 20:25.432
-Move in?
-Yeah, move in.

20:27.309 --> 20:30.437
Ever since I heard about you
living in that budget micro-unit.

20:30.520 --> 20:31.688
It's been on my mind.

20:35.234 --> 20:37.778
Sorry, I told him about your place.

20:39.655 --> 20:42.950
You wouldn't be a burden,
so just come live with us, okay?

20:43.450 --> 20:46.828
His sister just happens to be moving out,
so we have a spare room.

20:47.371 --> 20:50.207
And Yun's mom is also on board, of course.

20:52.334 --> 20:55.504
As adults, it's our duty and reward

20:55.587 --> 20:58.048
to support smart kids like you.

20:59.216 --> 21:01.551
So don't worry about it.
Just move in, okay?

21:02.469 --> 21:03.345
Eat up.

21:04.513 --> 21:07.349
Consider it your home
and come live with us.

21:12.980 --> 21:13.855
And

21:15.440 --> 21:16.316
you agreed?

21:16.400 --> 21:17.609
Of course.

21:18.110 --> 21:20.070
Saving on rent is a huge deal for me.

21:21.113 --> 21:23.323
And it'd be good for our lessons too.

21:23.407 --> 21:25.784
I could write about
what I see and feel every day.

21:27.244 --> 21:32.749
Still, letting someone into their home
can't be an easy thing for them.

21:32.833 --> 21:37.296
You think I don't know that?
That's what makes Mr. Kim so amazing.

21:38.255 --> 21:40.173
Se-yun told me later

21:40.757 --> 21:43.510
that his mom only agreed
because his dad was so adamant.

21:44.845 --> 21:48.307
Se-yun says he respects his dad
more than anyone else in the world.

21:49.224 --> 21:50.892
He's strong yet considerate

21:51.810 --> 21:53.812
and has a young, flexible mindset.

21:55.063 --> 21:57.274
Mr. Kim is a really admirable guy.

21:59.693 --> 22:01.528
I think he's the first adult I've met…

22:04.031 --> 22:05.282
that I want to be like.

22:11.663 --> 22:14.750
You've got a long way to go
if you want to be a writer.

22:15.250 --> 22:16.084
Sorry?

22:16.168 --> 22:19.421
You're too hasty
to make up your mind about people.

22:19.504 --> 22:21.340
And your judgment is shallow and simple.

22:21.840 --> 22:24.885
You think he's great, amazing,
and you want to be like him

22:24.968 --> 22:27.095
just because of that one thing?

22:31.224 --> 22:32.309
All right, fine.

22:32.976 --> 22:35.395
You're still young,
so I guess it's understandable.

22:35.479 --> 22:36.646
But…

22:40.025 --> 22:41.735
you should know this.

22:43.195 --> 22:48.283
So far, you've only seen that man
and his family at a surface level.

22:48.784 --> 22:51.745
A perfect middle-class family
that lacks nothing.

22:52.245 --> 22:55.707
It's obvious and cliché.
A textbook example.

22:57.209 --> 23:00.754
Do you know why that is?
Because that's how you want to see them.

23:01.880 --> 23:03.673
That's what you want them to be.

23:07.803 --> 23:08.970
When it comes to people,

23:09.471 --> 23:11.223
what matters isn't who they are.

23:11.723 --> 23:14.768
It's their relationships.
That's what you need to look out for.

23:15.268 --> 23:18.021
That's the only way
to see their true selves.

23:20.649 --> 23:23.026
Since you've already decided to move in…

23:25.445 --> 23:26.738
for now…

23:28.990 --> 23:32.411
start with Mr. Kim
and study his various relationships.

23:32.494 --> 23:34.246
Observe them closely.

23:35.247 --> 23:36.832
This is your first assignment.

23:37.457 --> 23:38.583
Okay.

23:43.547 --> 23:44.381
Eat up.

23:47.300 --> 23:50.720
Weren't you just envious of that dad?

23:51.721 --> 23:53.140
What do you mean "envious"?

23:54.391 --> 23:55.308
Well,

23:55.809 --> 23:59.604
because Lee Kang kept complimenting him,

24:00.147 --> 24:02.691
saying he was the first adult
he wanted to be like.

24:03.191 --> 24:04.901
Maybe you were just envious.

24:05.527 --> 24:06.695
Am I wrong?

24:07.446 --> 24:08.321
Hey, wait.

24:08.822 --> 24:12.451
What do you take me for?
Do you think I'm that childish?

24:13.034 --> 24:15.912
If not, then fine.
That's just what it sounded like to me.

24:15.996 --> 24:18.874
Were you eavesdropping again?
How much did you hear?

24:19.374 --> 24:21.585
I didn't mean to listen in.

24:21.668 --> 24:23.837
I just caught bits here and there.

24:26.798 --> 24:29.718
I was just saying what needed to be said.

24:29.801 --> 24:34.181
He was being too one-sided,
so I restored balance, as his teacher.

24:35.015 --> 24:36.016
That's true.

24:36.516 --> 24:39.644
To someone who's starved for attention,
such kindness can feel huge.

24:39.728 --> 24:41.354
And it is a pretty big deal.

24:43.315 --> 24:45.025
You could try being nicer to him too.

24:45.525 --> 24:48.904
I know you want him
to look up to you as an adult.

24:50.155 --> 24:53.366
That Lee Kang kid is actually pretty cute.

24:53.450 --> 24:55.076
He has a peculiar charm.

24:59.206 --> 25:01.458
But doesn't he look familiar?

25:03.543 --> 25:05.378
Earlier, when I first saw him…

25:07.214 --> 25:08.590
Hello, nice to meet you.

25:10.217 --> 25:12.511
Oh my, you shouldn't have.

25:13.178 --> 25:15.263
It's nice to meet you. Come on in.

25:22.312 --> 25:23.146
I don't know.

25:31.404 --> 25:34.658
So did Lee Kang say
whether it was true or not?

25:35.158 --> 25:36.785
What he wrote in his assignment.

25:37.494 --> 25:39.621
Why are you so interested?

25:40.205 --> 25:41.456
Ever the therapist.

25:41.540 --> 25:43.083
I know, right?

25:43.667 --> 25:45.544
It keeps weighing on my mind.

25:46.461 --> 25:51.341
I wonder if his childhood was even harder
than his writing implies,

25:51.424 --> 25:52.509
given his deflection.

25:53.301 --> 25:55.470
Who knows what that kid is thinking?

25:56.888 --> 25:59.891
You don't think he'll do something strange
at that house, do you?

26:02.769 --> 26:05.188
Never mind. It's just the therapist in me.

26:05.814 --> 26:06.898
Something strange?

26:07.482 --> 26:08.358
Like what?

26:09.693 --> 26:12.654
Well, you know how people are.

26:13.572 --> 26:15.156
They can only endure

26:15.240 --> 26:19.077
because they have people
who believe in them and support them.

26:19.578 --> 26:23.790
And their sense of ethics tends to be
determined by those relationships.

26:24.499 --> 26:27.586
It seems like he hasn't had
anyone like that in his life.

26:29.087 --> 26:31.172
I'm just concerned.

26:32.257 --> 26:35.468
Lonely people can become
a dangerous presence

26:36.052 --> 26:38.430
when put in certain situations.

26:39.139 --> 26:40.348
It's sad.

26:44.603 --> 26:46.104
A dangerous presence?

26:47.105 --> 26:48.023
Yes.

26:49.441 --> 26:50.692
What are you doing?

26:51.484 --> 26:53.945
Mr. Heo, look here.

26:54.029 --> 26:57.157
I made this game. Want to take a look?

26:58.658 --> 27:02.495
You press down to move forward
and double-click to do this.

28:00.762 --> 28:02.013
Some dream.

28:16.194 --> 28:18.488
Hello, I'm Lee Kang--

28:31.501 --> 28:34.129
There you are.
Well done for making it here.

28:34.629 --> 28:35.547
Here. Let me.

28:36.047 --> 28:38.591
The reason a trip is considered a trip…

28:44.514 --> 28:46.349
is because you have a home to return to.

28:57.318 --> 28:58.737
But this is your sister's room.

28:58.820 --> 29:02.657
I told you she moved out.
She only comes home a few times a year.

29:03.366 --> 29:04.325
It's your room now.

29:06.995 --> 29:07.829
All yours.

29:16.212 --> 29:19.257
Are you sure you'll be okay here?
We don't even use this room.

29:20.049 --> 29:21.176
It's fine.

29:23.178 --> 29:25.597
We should clear some of the junk out.

29:26.389 --> 29:29.225
And because you have
your own room to return to.

29:29.934 --> 29:32.479
I thought it'd upset her
if her room was gone.

29:32.562 --> 29:35.857
It was an easy decision
when I put myself in her shoes.

29:36.983 --> 29:38.693
Goodness, how sweet of you.

29:38.777 --> 29:40.779
And you're so considerate.

29:40.862 --> 29:42.655
You've never even met her.

29:43.448 --> 29:46.951
It's still a hundred times better
than my old place. I couldn't be happier.

29:47.619 --> 29:49.412
All right, then. A welcome toast.

29:50.705 --> 29:51.623
Lee Kang,

29:52.207 --> 29:53.708
welcome to the family.

29:53.792 --> 29:55.126
Welcome.

29:55.210 --> 29:56.419
Welcome!

29:59.172 --> 30:00.715
Speak of the devil.

30:01.216 --> 30:03.176
-It's Jeong-hu.
-Of course it is.

30:05.178 --> 30:07.347
I'm so nice,
I'm letting you keep your room.

30:08.056 --> 30:10.809
Whatever. I told you I don't care.

30:11.309 --> 30:14.395
This is my room and my home now.

30:14.479 --> 30:15.522
There you go again.

30:15.605 --> 30:18.817
You're going to make your dad cry.
He'll start crying from heartbreak.

30:18.900 --> 30:21.152
That's right, kid.
You're not family anymore.

30:21.778 --> 30:23.655
Just say hi. This is my friend.

30:24.405 --> 30:26.032
-Lee Kang?
-Hello.

30:27.700 --> 30:31.496
Hey. Yun's told me so much about you.
I feel like we've already met.

30:33.081 --> 30:34.791
-See you around.
-Sure.

30:35.708 --> 30:38.002
-Don't skip any meals.
-Bye.

30:38.086 --> 30:41.714
It's because you have people
who welcome you when you're back.

30:42.215 --> 30:43.424
Dad!

30:43.508 --> 30:45.510
Does that mean I can now

30:46.135 --> 30:47.846
go on a trip too?

30:49.264 --> 30:52.559
Can I finally set off on a trip of my own?

31:11.578 --> 31:13.496
What are you looking at, jerk?

31:13.580 --> 31:15.832
Thanks to you, I now have more work to do.

31:24.674 --> 31:27.093
The one person
who's ruining the thrill of a new trip.

31:31.264 --> 31:33.558
I heard you lived in a budget micro-unit.

31:34.851 --> 31:36.227
Guess you struck gold.

31:45.361 --> 31:46.613
Her name is Seon Min-hui.

31:46.696 --> 31:48.656
She's in her early-thirties, maybe?

31:48.740 --> 31:50.867
She comes to work three times a week.

31:59.292 --> 32:00.710
Oh my gosh! Oh dear.

32:01.753 --> 32:02.879
Sorry.

32:02.962 --> 32:04.672
You should be more careful.

32:04.756 --> 32:06.174
It's okay. I'll do it.

32:12.680 --> 32:16.225
She's the only person
who hates that I moved into this house.

32:16.309 --> 32:20.396
You can't throw your cigarette butts
in the flower bed. This is yours, right?

32:21.314 --> 32:22.565
It isn't.

32:23.274 --> 32:24.609
It's not mine, it's his.

32:24.692 --> 32:26.986
You know, that friend of Se-yun's.
Lee Kang.

32:27.528 --> 32:28.488
I saw him do it.

32:28.988 --> 32:32.450
What are you talking about?
Now you're even telling lies?

32:32.533 --> 32:35.411
Here, there's clearly lipstick on it.

32:36.120 --> 32:38.122
Besides, our kids don't smoke.

32:39.415 --> 32:42.961
As smoking is a preference,
I can't do anything about it, but still.

32:43.628 --> 32:46.005
I don't want anyone smoking in my home.

32:46.506 --> 32:48.091
It's bad for the flowers too.

32:49.425 --> 32:51.010
Please don't, okay?

32:59.686 --> 33:00.520
What?

33:01.312 --> 33:02.939
Bad for the flowers, you say?

33:42.979 --> 33:45.023
Just hire someone else.

33:45.106 --> 33:46.899
Why are you putting up with her?

33:47.400 --> 33:49.485
I can tell her for you
if you find it hard.

33:49.986 --> 33:51.112
Oh, I don't know.

33:52.447 --> 33:54.490
I don't know what to do with her.

33:54.991 --> 33:57.535
I felt bad for her
because she's a single mother.

33:58.453 --> 34:00.705
But if I fire her,

34:01.205 --> 34:04.042
I couldn't face the president
of our church's volunteer group.

34:04.125 --> 34:05.752
They introduced her to me.

34:06.669 --> 34:10.923
You're overthinking things so much,
it's making you cranky.

34:11.924 --> 34:12.800
Legs here.

34:17.263 --> 34:18.598
Still,

34:20.099 --> 34:21.893
she might be a bit unruly,

34:22.518 --> 34:24.896
but her side dishes are incredible.

34:25.646 --> 34:28.733
Our Yun devours
all the side dishes Min-hui makes.

34:29.650 --> 34:30.651
That's good.

34:31.152 --> 34:34.072
That feels so good. That's the spot.

34:34.155 --> 34:34.989
Here?

34:35.656 --> 34:36.783
I'm good at this, right?

34:37.366 --> 34:38.451
You sure are.

34:39.077 --> 34:40.953
You get better by the day.

34:42.246 --> 34:43.873
You're as good as any masseuse.

34:50.171 --> 34:51.339
So,

34:52.006 --> 34:53.674
please don't think too much.

34:53.758 --> 34:56.094
Don't let useless thoughts
clutter your mind, okay?

34:57.595 --> 35:01.307
The most important thing to me
is that you feel at peace, okay?

35:02.141 --> 35:03.226
In our family,

35:04.393 --> 35:06.562
nothing matters more than that.

35:07.605 --> 35:09.899
Oh, all right.

35:09.982 --> 35:12.193
I can't say anything to you
without you worrying.

36:00.032 --> 36:01.701
You know the kids are home, right?

36:02.201 --> 36:03.703
So what if they are?

36:38.070 --> 36:38.905
You didn't…

36:41.616 --> 36:43.117
listen in on that, did you?

36:44.202 --> 36:45.703
No, Se-yun called me

36:46.746 --> 36:48.289
not long after that.

36:54.003 --> 36:56.088
Why do you look so disappointed?

36:56.631 --> 36:57.465
Sorry?

37:01.510 --> 37:02.345
Hey.

37:02.845 --> 37:03.971
Don't.

37:05.139 --> 37:07.266
That's voyeurism, you know.

37:08.517 --> 37:11.604
I told you to be an observer,
not a voyeur.

37:12.647 --> 37:13.856
That's unacceptable.

37:15.233 --> 37:16.359
What's the difference?

37:16.442 --> 37:17.777
The difference, you punk…

37:19.779 --> 37:20.738
Hold on.

37:30.498 --> 37:31.791
What are you doing?

37:39.757 --> 37:42.301
Deliberately spying on
and eavesdropping on people.

37:42.385 --> 37:46.472
Anyway, the moment you start
indulging in it, it becomes voyeurism.

37:47.598 --> 37:49.517
I didn't see them on purpose.

37:50.393 --> 37:51.727
It just happened.

37:53.187 --> 37:54.563
You sly bastard.

37:55.898 --> 37:57.733
Do you honestly think that's believable?

37:59.944 --> 38:02.238
Absolutely not. Observation only.

38:03.864 --> 38:07.326
Anyway, Mr. Kim really loves his wife.

38:07.410 --> 38:08.953
That's my point.

38:09.036 --> 38:11.038
From what I've observed,

38:12.623 --> 38:15.334
the two of them
frequently share small touches.

38:15.835 --> 38:19.630
Do you think two people being touchy-feely
always means it's love?

38:19.714 --> 38:21.632
If it's not love, what is it?

38:21.716 --> 38:26.178
Okay, yeah. You're still young,
so you might see that as love.

38:26.679 --> 38:29.932
But you see, with married couples…

38:34.020 --> 38:37.148
it could very well be a desperate attempt

38:38.357 --> 38:40.526
to overcome the cold tedium

38:42.111 --> 38:43.529
that has settled over time.

38:43.612 --> 38:46.032
What am I even saying right now?

38:48.284 --> 38:51.579
Anyway, married couples
are complicated, okay?

38:52.079 --> 38:53.664
Are you talking about yourself?

38:55.416 --> 38:56.250
What?

38:57.418 --> 39:00.880
Well, I'm just wondering
how things are with you and your wife.

39:02.048 --> 39:04.508
Why are you curious about that?

39:06.302 --> 39:07.261
You little punk.

39:07.762 --> 39:10.473
You stepped on the line. Don't cross it.

39:14.143 --> 39:17.980
Hey, tell me more about that housekeeper.

39:18.064 --> 39:19.565
No, I don't want to.

39:20.483 --> 39:22.109
I don't want to talk about her.

39:22.193 --> 39:23.444
Why not?

39:24.737 --> 39:26.155
Does she keep harassing you?

39:27.490 --> 39:29.533
Tell me about you instead. Please?

39:31.660 --> 39:32.578
Do the two of you…

39:34.830 --> 39:35.998
love each other?

39:36.540 --> 39:40.211
How do we seem to you?
Do we look like we're in love?

39:40.294 --> 39:42.671
Why would you ask something like that?

39:42.755 --> 39:45.424
You're talking nonsense
and to a little kid at that.

39:45.925 --> 39:48.677
What do you mean "a little kid"?
He's an adult now.

39:49.178 --> 39:52.348
And he's at the age where he'd be curious
about these things, right?

39:53.516 --> 39:56.811
It seems like you love Mr. Heo,

39:58.270 --> 39:59.980
but I'm not sure about Mr. Heo.

40:02.900 --> 40:06.529
You're right.
I always wonder about him too.

40:07.446 --> 40:08.906
You tell me. Do you love me?

40:11.742 --> 40:12.743
Hey.

40:12.827 --> 40:14.578
Stop eating. Put that down.

40:16.038 --> 40:18.791
What are you doing?
Our lesson ended ages ago.

40:18.874 --> 40:19.708
Hurry on home.

40:19.792 --> 40:23.504
What's your deal?
I ordered this specifically for Kang.

40:24.004 --> 40:25.381
Take your time and eat up.

40:26.132 --> 40:27.550
You should have some too.

40:29.135 --> 40:30.136
You too, Mr. Heo.

40:30.219 --> 40:31.345
I am.

40:34.265 --> 40:37.852
Then maybe I'll try a piece too.

40:40.020 --> 40:42.314
No, I need to lose weight.

40:42.815 --> 40:44.442
You're trying to lose weight?

40:45.109 --> 40:47.236
But you're already so beautiful.

40:47.736 --> 40:48.988
Oh my, is that right?

40:52.366 --> 40:55.744
Thank you. You're the only one
who compliments me like that.

40:58.247 --> 40:59.957
What a load of crap.

41:05.713 --> 41:09.633
The truth is,
I think Mr. Heo loves you too.

41:10.134 --> 41:12.887
Maybe his love is so deep
that it's invisible.

41:12.970 --> 41:14.013
You think so?

41:14.763 --> 41:16.307
What makes you think that?

41:17.683 --> 41:19.727
I finished reading Mr. Heo's book.

41:21.645 --> 41:25.733
After reading it,
I realized who the one woman is.

41:27.902 --> 41:28.903
The one woman?

41:29.612 --> 41:31.655
Mr. Heo told me in a previous lesson

41:32.156 --> 41:36.577
that the 12 women are just symbolic,
and it's actually about one woman.

41:36.660 --> 41:37.786
When did I say that?

41:38.746 --> 41:39.663
When did I say that?

41:40.164 --> 41:41.457
You said that.

41:42.082 --> 41:44.543
You said it quietly,
but I definitely heard you.

41:45.044 --> 41:46.295
I'm guessing that one woman

41:47.546 --> 41:49.757
is Ms. Jo, of course.

41:51.091 --> 41:51.926
Right?

41:56.263 --> 41:57.389
One woman?

42:12.279 --> 42:16.242
Hey, don't pay any mind
to what that kid said as a joke.

42:16.325 --> 42:19.036
That kid was just spouting nonsense.

42:19.119 --> 42:20.287
Don't worry about it.

42:20.788 --> 42:22.414
Worry? Please.

42:22.998 --> 42:25.543
Your age-old first love? What a laugh.

42:27.962 --> 42:29.213
What? First love?

42:30.422 --> 42:31.757
It's that woman.

42:31.840 --> 42:35.636
The name that keeps coming up
in your old draft notes.

42:36.262 --> 42:37.555
It must be her.

42:38.347 --> 42:40.724
That's all in the past. Ancient history.

42:41.350 --> 42:43.394
What does any of that matter now?

42:44.228 --> 42:46.146
Yeah, I didn't say anything about it.

42:47.648 --> 42:48.566
Still,

42:49.441 --> 42:52.736
I didn't know all 12 women were her.

42:53.487 --> 42:58.200
Then again, what do I even know about you?

43:09.003 --> 43:09.962
Lee Kang.

43:10.462 --> 43:12.339
That little smart-ass, I swear…

43:16.885 --> 43:19.888
It doesn't always take a typhoon
to sway a tree.

43:24.101 --> 43:26.145
Some trees can be uprooted

43:26.645 --> 43:28.731
with a mere passing breeze.

43:29.982 --> 43:32.818
Why do you keep suspecting me?

43:32.901 --> 43:35.571
I told you, I didn't steal it!

43:35.654 --> 43:38.574
Why are you lying to me again
when I found it right here?

43:38.657 --> 43:40.993
Then how else would it have
ended up in here?

43:41.493 --> 43:43.412
How should I know?

43:44.121 --> 43:45.164
And also,

43:45.998 --> 43:48.334
why would you go through my bag
without permission?

43:49.668 --> 43:51.795
I'm sorry about that.

43:52.296 --> 43:54.381
But do you really think I wanted to look?

43:54.465 --> 43:56.717
I searched everywhere.
I was at my wits' end!

43:56.800 --> 43:59.595
Why is it pouring all of a sudden?

44:02.931 --> 44:06.935
So what if your damn scarf is designer?

44:08.979 --> 44:12.524
If you keep doubting me like this,

44:13.317 --> 44:15.277
I won't be able to work here anymore.

44:16.737 --> 44:17.571
I quit.

44:25.579 --> 44:27.247
What's the matter this time?

44:27.748 --> 44:28.707
Well,

44:29.208 --> 44:30.876
Min-hui stole my new scarf…

44:31.794 --> 44:33.545
Mom!

44:34.672 --> 44:35.589
Are you okay?

44:36.090 --> 44:38.801
-Should I bring you your sedatives?
-Yeah, get me my meds.

44:38.884 --> 44:40.052
Yeah, okay.

44:43.722 --> 44:47.810
This is why I told you not to stress
and just hire someone else!

44:49.687 --> 44:50.854
Damn it.

44:52.147 --> 44:54.191
That's it. I'll have a firm word with her.

44:54.274 --> 44:55.484
Honey…

45:00.948 --> 45:02.324
Are you out of your mind?

45:06.203 --> 45:10.207
You've gone beyond being a voyeur
and are actually messing with them now?

45:12.042 --> 45:12.960
You're telling me

45:14.461 --> 45:16.505
you snuck the scarf in her bag?

45:18.966 --> 45:20.300
I did,

45:20.801 --> 45:22.594
but she messed with me first.

45:22.678 --> 45:25.597
She spilled drinks on me on purpose
and kept belittling me.

45:25.681 --> 45:27.641
You think this is on the same level?

45:28.600 --> 45:29.435
So, what?

45:30.144 --> 45:31.812
You wanted to get her fired?

45:32.688 --> 45:34.857
No, I was just pulling a prank--

45:34.940 --> 45:37.484
A prank? What do you mean "prank"?

45:38.944 --> 45:40.154
What you did

45:40.988 --> 45:42.990
was frame someone as a thief.

45:43.907 --> 45:44.950
You crossed a line.

45:48.912 --> 45:50.748
I wouldn't have done that

45:51.373 --> 45:53.083
if she hadn't messed with me.

45:58.881 --> 46:00.382
You punk, you really…

46:00.883 --> 46:03.802
You go around causing trouble
with every family you visit!

46:06.263 --> 46:07.264
Every family?

46:11.935 --> 46:13.687
Look, kid, what I mean is…

46:14.605 --> 46:16.690
I told you over and over again, didn't I?

46:17.274 --> 46:22.821
I told you to observe relationships,
not to go around sparking conflict.

46:22.905 --> 46:23.906
Right?

46:24.656 --> 46:26.700
Meddling and starting arguments.

46:27.659 --> 46:29.328
A writer shouldn't do that.

46:31.997 --> 46:35.918
After our last lesson, did you argue
with your wife because of what I…

46:38.462 --> 46:40.297
Is that why we're here today for--

46:40.380 --> 46:44.092
Argue? We didn't argue!
Don't act like you know everything!

46:48.096 --> 46:49.014
Anyway,

46:49.890 --> 46:52.392
our lessons will take place here
from now on. Period.

46:53.477 --> 46:54.311
Yes, sir.

46:57.439 --> 46:59.149
Man, I'm exhausted.

47:00.067 --> 47:02.611
Let's call it a day.
We'll continue next time.

47:07.866 --> 47:08.992
But, Mr. Heo,

47:09.701 --> 47:11.078
I learned a shocking truth.

47:11.161 --> 47:14.039
I was going to write it,
but I wanted to tell you in person.

47:17.167 --> 47:19.086
You were right, Mr. Heo.

47:20.420 --> 47:22.798
You can't judge a person by what you see.

47:23.674 --> 47:24.675
Keep it short.

47:25.551 --> 47:28.178
There's something going on
between Mr. Kim and Min-hui.

47:32.057 --> 47:32.891
That day…

47:34.518 --> 47:36.186
I saw them that day.

47:43.068 --> 47:47.364
Mr. Kim stepped outside, saying he'd have
a firm word with Min-hui, but…

48:08.886 --> 48:10.804
they looked like a couple.

48:13.807 --> 48:17.936
Then Se-yun's dad grabbed her,
and they went into the garage.

48:18.020 --> 48:21.148
So I secretly followed them,
and I saw… I saw…

48:43.462 --> 48:45.505
the car was shaking.

48:45.589 --> 48:47.883
Shaking like this.
What else could that mean?

48:47.966 --> 48:48.967
Hey!

48:52.512 --> 48:54.014
Is this why you moved in?

48:54.514 --> 48:57.184
To spy on them and make assumptions?

48:57.684 --> 49:01.355
Do you think I'm giving you these lessons
so I can listen to this bullshit?

49:01.438 --> 49:03.482
No, I really saw it!

49:03.565 --> 49:04.900
You saw it? Really?

49:04.983 --> 49:07.694
You said you felt dizzy that day.
Are you sure you saw that?

49:07.778 --> 49:09.404
Yes, of course I saw…

49:15.661 --> 49:16.536
Lee Kang.

49:17.663 --> 49:19.206
What you're saying right now

49:19.748 --> 49:24.962
is no different from indiscriminately
swinging a hammer at people.

49:25.462 --> 49:26.964
Just like in that game you made.

49:27.047 --> 49:29.675
That unethical
and irresponsible attitude of yours.

49:29.758 --> 49:32.302
Caring only for entertainment
regardless of the truth!

49:35.722 --> 49:36.807
But the thing is…

49:38.850 --> 49:40.644
literature is not a game.

49:42.646 --> 49:45.691
Your attitude must be sincere.
That's of the utmost importance.

49:48.819 --> 49:50.529
In order to write a good story,

49:52.114 --> 49:53.949
you have to be a decent human being.

49:56.660 --> 49:57.494
Got it?

50:07.796 --> 50:09.589
I think you were right.

50:16.346 --> 50:17.556
Lee Kang, that punk.

50:19.391 --> 50:22.310
I think there's something off
about that bastard.

50:23.186 --> 50:24.896
I think I need to stop the lessons.

50:29.317 --> 50:32.320
Isn't that why you liked him?
Because he was stimulating?

50:33.155 --> 50:34.489
I quite like him.

50:35.907 --> 50:37.242
What the heck?

50:38.160 --> 50:40.245
You said he was dangerous and all that.

50:42.039 --> 50:43.707
That was your takeaway?

50:44.791 --> 50:46.460
Such poor comprehension skills.

50:46.543 --> 50:47.377
What?

50:48.295 --> 50:50.338
I was just briefly worried.

50:51.256 --> 50:52.924
But I'm not worried anymore.

50:53.800 --> 50:56.136
He seems more normal than you.

51:00.807 --> 51:02.851
What? Are you still…

51:04.227 --> 51:05.812
Am I still what?

51:06.354 --> 51:08.774
I have a lot of reports to write.
Please leave.

51:53.568 --> 52:00.575
LEE KANG

52:12.838 --> 52:13.672
What is it?

52:14.172 --> 52:15.382
Were you sleeping?

52:15.882 --> 52:18.260
I'm so sorry, but I got into an accident.

52:18.844 --> 52:20.929
I need a guardian, so could you…

52:21.638 --> 52:23.390
Could you please come here?

52:23.890 --> 52:25.308
What? An accident?

52:25.809 --> 52:29.646
You'll get the details when you're here.
It's urgent, so please hurry.

52:31.439 --> 52:32.524
But

52:33.150 --> 52:34.317
why did you contact me?

52:34.401 --> 52:36.611
You were the first person
who came to mind.

52:36.695 --> 52:38.321
I could have called Mr. Kim,

52:38.905 --> 52:41.992
but still, I'd like for you to come.

52:48.498 --> 52:50.625
Fine. Where are you?

53:19.529 --> 53:20.447
What's going on?

53:24.326 --> 53:25.911
What accident, exactly?

53:27.495 --> 53:28.496
I'm sorry.

53:29.581 --> 53:30.665
The truth is…

53:35.503 --> 53:36.546
Did you lie to me?

53:36.630 --> 53:38.298
I'll tell you everything.

53:38.381 --> 53:39.424
The truth is…

53:39.507 --> 53:40.425
Look over there.

53:40.926 --> 53:42.385
Just now,

53:42.469 --> 53:44.638
Mr. Kim and Min-hui went into that hotel.

53:45.138 --> 53:47.015
I saw them by chance and followed them.

53:51.770 --> 53:53.730
I wanted you to see it for yourself,

53:54.773 --> 53:56.274
since you wouldn't believe me.

53:58.318 --> 53:59.236
Mr. Heo!

53:59.778 --> 54:01.988
I told you, I saw them!
Why won't you believe me?

54:02.072 --> 54:03.782
Fine, you punk!

54:04.282 --> 54:06.493
Let's say you did see them. So what?

54:06.993 --> 54:10.247
What does such vulgar gossip
have to do with me?

54:12.999 --> 54:15.877
You dragged me here for this crap,
by lying, no less?

54:18.296 --> 54:19.381
I'm done with you.

54:19.464 --> 54:21.341
I can't waste any more of my time

54:21.841 --> 54:23.927
on this foolishness.

54:25.887 --> 54:28.932
I don't need this. Our lessons are over.

54:29.432 --> 54:30.558
Over!

54:34.813 --> 54:35.647
Oh my God!

54:35.730 --> 54:36.815
What the…

54:40.360 --> 54:42.570
Oh no, she's bleeding. Hurry!

55:06.553 --> 55:07.846
That's her.

55:10.307 --> 55:11.308
Min-hui.

55:12.767 --> 55:13.643
What did you say?

55:14.144 --> 55:15.520
An ambulance. Hurry!

55:23.528 --> 55:24.529
That's Mr. Kim.

55:25.030 --> 55:27.365
-She's bleeding.
-Where?

55:41.046 --> 55:41.880
That…

55:42.630 --> 55:44.883
That man is…

55:47.093 --> 55:48.303
Mr. Kim?

55:49.387 --> 55:50.680
Se-yun's dad?

55:52.724 --> 55:53.558
Yes.

56:19.250 --> 56:20.168
That man…

56:22.128 --> 56:23.296
is Mr. Kim?

56:48.863 --> 56:52.367
So you're Se-yun's new friend.
Nice to meet you. Lee Kang, right?

57:15.056 --> 57:16.307
Kim Su-hun.

57:17.934 --> 57:19.310
Kim Su-hun…

57:25.191 --> 57:26.609
is Se-yun's dad?

58:13.198 --> 58:16.201
NOTES FROM THE LAST ROW

01:00:42.305 --> 01:00:47.310
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
